    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔβενος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ
			</span>(ὁ in <i><span class="en">
			<u>BCH</u>
			35.286
		</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>)), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ebony</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.97
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.123
			</span></i>:—being the black heart-wood of various species of
			Diospyrus, 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. Αἰθιοπική</span>, =
			<i>D. mespiliformis</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.
			Ἰνδική</span>, =
			<i>D. Ebenum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.98
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				384b17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.5.4
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐβένη, ἡ</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.4.6
			</span></i>). (Prob. an Egyptian word.)</div>
